#ASSERT `s 790LT(2) the officer of the entity who is in default also commits the offence` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) summary conviction: (a) England and Wales, a fine; (b) Scotland or Northern Ireland, a fine not exceeding level 5 and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5
#ASSERT `s 790LT(3) the penalty` `on summary conviction in England and Wales` EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 790LT(3) the penalty` `on summary conviction in Scotland` EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1), `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 790LT(3) the penalty` `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1), `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 790LT(3) the penalty` `on conviction on indictment` EQUALS NOTHING
